# ldeluipy.es — project preferences

Live at `https://ldeluipy.es`. Pure HTML/CSS/JS (no frameworks, no Node/npm build). Accent `#0f0`. Design follows Hallmark (anti-AI-slop); respect existing tokens and `primordial.css` when present.

## Tone & CTAs

- Prefer **Contáctame / Contactar**, never **Contrátame / Contratar** (too aggressive).
- No `mailto:` links. Contact section uses copy-to-clipboard for the email (or Discord / other non-mailto CTAs).
- Copy stays honest: no invented metrics, fake testimonials, or static headcounts that go stale (e.g. avoid “20+ services”).

## Capability / “Qué hago” copy

Keep **generic and adaptable**, not a stack laundry list:

- Product: study the problem; pick or adapt to the best tech — no sacred stack.
- Automation: bots that remove busywork; connect to whatever tool they already use (Discord, their tracker, any API) — avoid locking copy to one product name (e.g. Redmine) unless the case study is that product.
- Infra: Linux servers, deploy, domains, security, monitoring — stay high-level. Skip Ubuntu/Apache/Let’s Encrypt jargon for a general audience; HTTPS-as-product-detail is redundant.

Tech marquee can list tools (and light easter eggs like Minecraft). Space words generously; hover must **ease** speed down/up, never hard-pause.

## Cases / map

- Section framing: **Casos reales**, not “Cosas reales”.
- Prefer live URLs when a project is up (e.g. Serra over dead/archived stand-ins).
- Ultron lives at `https://github.com/AMVARA-CONSULTING/ultron-redmine` (repo moved off Luipy56).
- Ecosystem map: capability layers (web / automation / infra), not a tech-name dump; no brittle static service counts on the hub node.

## Deploy & sync

- DocumentRoot for the apex is `/var/www/ldeluipy.es`. After edits here, keep `vault.ldeluipy.es/ldeluipy.es/` in sync if that mirror still exists.
- Do not expose tooling dirs (`.cursor`, `.hallmark`, `.git`) via Apache.
- Commits: author **Luipy56**; commit messages must not mention AI tooling.
